From: Plain Browser
Subject: [safebrowsing] Use the public phishing list (SOCIAL_ENGINEERING_PUBLIC)

Category: 70-safebrowsing. Applies after 0001 (same file). With the Chrome-only SOCIAL_ENGINEERING list in the
request Google answers 403 "ThreatType is not accessible" for the whole update; with SOCIAL_ENGINEERING_PUBLIC
the identical request returns 200 (verified 2026-10-26 through sb.plain-browser.app with the request taken from
a NetLog). The local store name and SBThreatType stay the same, so lookups and UI are unchanged.
---
--- a/components/safe_browsing/core/browser/db/sb_protocol_manager_util.cc
+++ b/components/safe_browsing/core/browser/db/sb_protocol_manager_util.cc
@@ -298,10 +298,13 @@
 }
 
 ListIdentifier GetUrlSocEngId() {
+  // Plain Browser: SOCIAL_ENGINEERING (5) is the Chrome-only phishing list;
+  // a third-party API key is served SOCIAL_ENGINEERING_PUBLIC (2). Asking for
+  // the former fails the whole list update ("ThreatType is not accessible").
   return base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(safe_browsing::kLocalListsUseSBv5)
              ? ListIdentifier(SBThreatType::SB_THREAT_TYPE_URL_PHISHING)
              : ListIdentifier(GetCurrentPlatformType(), URL,
-                              SOCIAL_ENGINEERING);
+                              SOCIAL_ENGINEERING_PUBLIC);
 }
 
 ListIdentifier GetUrlSubresourceFilterId() {
